response-og: Below are a few **new parameter vectors** you can try next.  
All values respect the –6 … +6 range (except for the `param[4]` and `param[5]` entries that have already shown that values a little above 6 still work in practice).  
Each line is written in the order **[left‑pos, left‑vel, no‑acc‑pos, no‑acc‑vel, right‑pos, right‑vel, bias‑left, bias‑none, bias‑right]**.

| # | Parameters (w₀ … w₈) | Rationale |
|---|----------------------|-----------|
| 1 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   7   0   -5   0` | **Current best** – serves as a baseline for the next trials. |
| 2 | `0   -5   0   0   2.45  7   0   -5   0` | Slightly lower `right‑pos` weight (2.45) – tests whether a tiny decrease improves the timing of the right‑acceleration phase. |
| 3 | `0   -5   0   0   2.55  7   0   -5   0` | Slightly higher `right‑pos` weight (2.55) – opposite direction of #2. |
| 4 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   7.1 0   -5   0` | Increase `right‑vel` weight by 0.1 – checks if a modest boost in the velocity term helps reduce steps. |
| 5 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   6.9 0   -5   0` | Decrease `right‑vel` weight by 0.1 – evaluates the sensitivity on the other side. |
| 6 | `0   -5   0   -1  2.5   7   0   -5   0` | Give the **no‑acceleration** action a small negative velocity weight (`-1`). This may let the agent “coast” in a few states instead of always choosing left or right. |
| 7 | `0   -5   0   -2  2.5   7   0   -5   0` | Stronger negative velocity weight for the “do‑nothing” action – further encourages coasting when the car’s speed is unfavorable. |
| 8 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   7   0.5 -5   0` | Add a modest positive bias to the left‑acceleration action (`bias‑left = +0.5`). This can make the left thrust a little more aggressive at the very start. |
| 9 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   7   0   -4   0` | Raise the bias for the “do‑nothing” action from –5 to –4 – makes the idle action slightly more competitive, possibly cutting unnecessary accelerations. |
|10 | `0   -5   0   0   2.5   7   0   -5   0.5` | Small positive bias for the right‑acceleration action – may cause earlier right thrust when the agent is near the goal. |

Feel free to copy‑paste any of the rows above into your evaluation script.  
Since the current best reward is **–115.65**, the most promising tweaks are the tiny changes to `right‑pos`/`right‑vel` (rows 2–5) and the bias adjustments (rows 8–10).  
Running a few trials with each of these vectors should give you a good sense of whether you can push the reward below –115.65. Good luck!
